        "like": 1
      },
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "To add to this issue related to this exact bug, my avatar base has both male and female anatomy, with dyn bone scripts for bust. \nRather than remove the component, i just unticked the script before upload. During autoconvert for old content, that component is toggled to 'on' when loaded, when it should be 'off' when loaded, resulting in avatar having phys active where they aren't intended.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-04-22T12:21:06.969Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "the current conversion of dynamic bones to physbones ignores all animations that reference the dynamicbone script and its settings. this has negatively affected a substantial amount of avatars with clothing, wings, tails, and tongues that toggle dynamicbones for animations. \nautoconversion would need to change the animation references to the physbone counterparts to solve this.\nit would need any referenced bones the check finds to also default to \"is animated\"\nthis affects rex, nargacuga, wickerbeast, and many more common avatars",
